Cancel a favorite on the lease alone: drop the tag predicate from the conditional skip.

The skip that cancels a hearted picture's upload must match only while the `favorites` tag is
absent AT STATEMENT TIME. Without the NOT EXISTS it trusts the revalidation read taken just before,
so a heart that landed in between — with the lease still standing, as when the heart's own enqueue
never ran — is cancelled anyway and the favorite never reaches the album. The interleaving (a)
probe that holds the lease and re-tags between the read and the skip must turn red; every other
probe in the module passes straight through it.

--- a/app/services/frame_share.py
+++ b/app/services/frame_share.py
@@ -551,7 +551,6 @@
                 FavoriteFrameJob.id == job.id,
                 FavoriteFrameJob.claimed_by == claimed_by,
                 FavoriteFrameJob.claimed_at == claimed_at,
-                ~_favorite_tag_present(FavoriteFrameJob.attachment_id),
             )
         )
         .values(state=FrameShareState.skipped, error=UNFAVORITED_ERROR)
